<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Tidore Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1450 CE – 1905 CE (approx.) · capital Soasio</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The clove sultanate of the North Moluccas, rival of Ternate and ally of Spain, which claimed authority over much of western New Guinea.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Tidore, a volcanic island just south of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ternate-sultanate">Ternate</a>, was one of the four Moluccan kingdoms known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moloku-kie-raha">Moloku Kie Raha</a>. Its rulers adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the late 15th century. In 1521 the surviving ships of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-magellan">Ferdinand Magellan's</a> expedition loaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a> at Tidore, beginning a long alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> against Ternate and the Portuguese.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tidore's wealth came from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a>, and its sultans claimed overlordship of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halmahera">Halmahera</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raja-ampat-islands">Raja Ampat</a> islands and coasts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, which sent tribute. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Saifuddin in the late 17th century it accepted the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dutch-east-india-company-territories">Dutch East India Company</a>. Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuku-of-tidore">Nuku</a> led a long revolt from 1780 and, with British help, briefly restored independence in 1801.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Tidore became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> dependency in the 19th century. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-independence">Indonesian independence</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zainal-abidin-syah">Zainal Abidin Syah</a> supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia's</a> claim to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-new-guinea">West New Guinea</a> and became its first governor. The sultanate survives as a cultural institution.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tidore-sultanate.jpg" alt="Tidore Sultanate" width="320" height="210"><figcaption>Image: Fazoffic · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Sultanate_of_Tidore.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1450 CE – 1905 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Soasio</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Saifuddin, Nuku, Zainal Abidin Syah</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tidore, Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/indonesia">Indonesia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sultanate of Tidore, Tidore</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1678&amp;focus=tidore-sultanate" aria-label="Tidore Sultanate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8224 2155 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tidore Sultanate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8544 2411L8309 1890M8544 2411L7959 2663M8544 2411L7959 2663"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8309 1890h0M7959 2663h0M7959 2663h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8544 2411h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8544 2411h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1678&amp;focus=tidore-sultanate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

